      {
        "id": 2920647,
        "name": "Marq Aideron",
        "username": "Marq_Aideron",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/marq_aideron/{size}/423243_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-08-31T14:11:05.974Z",
        "cooked": "<p>v2.4.1 is released.  This was a quick hotfix ontop of v2.4.0 which brought about sales tracking and profit distribution with a versioned policy manager.  I also included a way to build out ‘paychecks’ for your members using this data with backend validation once the money transfer actually happens.</p>\n<p>We’re currently rethinking the assignment workflow and priorities keep shifting as we use the app.  I believe the next step is rethinking the profit distribution to be a bit more fair in payouts.  Our first cycle of 2.4.1 turned out to pay people quite disproportionately as I had figured would happen but I didn’t think it would be this bad.  The next iteration will take all builder profits and put them in a pool then distribute equally amongst the builders.  Still a work in progress and maybe we keep it so that both paths are viable with a switch control in the policy builder.</p>\n<p>More to come as I find time and energy to put into it but at this stage its mostly feature complete for what we want/need.  As I play with the data and ask my AI questions I’ll slowly build out more features and admin functions for monitoring the state of the industry underneath.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
